WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.630
- Alright, I always like to end the show

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:02.920
with something happy and uplifting.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.192
This is 'What I'm Liking.'

00:00:05.192 --> 00:00:07.870
(upbeat sound effect)

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.870
Earlier this hour, we met
Craig, a music teacher

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.850
who had a major impact on
his former student, Talia.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.234
She's now starring in
'Wicked' on Broadway.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.630
(imitates air horn)

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.247
Music teachers make a difference, y'all.

00:00:19.247 --> 00:00:20.930
It did in my life as well.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.770
But now I want you to meet Katy Dane.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.630
She's a middle school music teacher

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.360
who was recently named
Music Educator of the Year

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.964
by the National Association
for Music Education

00:00:29.964 --> 00:00:32.760
and the Barbershop Harmony Society.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.339
She's also a fellow Texan,

00:00:34.339 --> 00:00:35.640
(imitates air horn)

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.460
and we have her on the line right now

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.777
watching on CBS, Austin.

00:00:39.777 --> 00:00:41.962
What's up, how you doing, Katy?

00:00:41.962 --> 00:00:44.448
(audience cheering)
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:44.448 --> 00:00:45.281
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:45.281 --> 00:00:48.445
Your choir room right now is
just taking me back, ma'am.

00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:49.860
That's amazing.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.380
- This is (indistinct), right?

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.250
- I mean, I don't know
we had all those trophies

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.980
but, yeah, look like
that, but congratulations.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.810
I think you have more jobs than I do.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.320
Can you tell everybody what you do?

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.810
- So I teach at Benold Middle School

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.890
and I teach sixth through eighth
grade orchestra and choir.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.960
And then I also direct
two a cappella groups

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.630
and one of them is A Cappella Unlimited

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.260
and that's through Sweet
Adelines International

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.230
and I'm on the regional
education team for that.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:17.240
And then I also direct a
a cappella Texas chorus,

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.180
Barbershop Chorus

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.330
and that's with Barbershop
Harmony Society.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.180
And I'm on the Southwestern District Board

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.340
for that in vocal performance and music.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.750
And then the other one
I do is Sing! Texas.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:32.750
And we do promotional
music and conferences,

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.760
concerts for students all the way,

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.860
sixth grade through twelfth grade

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.460
in collegiate a cappella

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.440
and help them with kind
of educational outreach

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.300
and that kind of thing.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.764
- Oh my gosh, you're doing all the things.

00:01:44.764 --> 00:01:45.680
(audience applauding)
I love it.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.367
I heard that you actually didn't even know

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:51.060
that you were nominated for this award.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.181
- No, it was totally a surprise to me.

00:01:53.181 --> 00:01:55.182
So it happened in early February

00:01:55.182 --> 00:01:58.190
and our Vice Principal came into the room

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:00.040
and kind of was a big storm

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.365
and she said, "we have
to evacuate the building.

00:02:01.365 --> 00:02:02.450
We have to get out."

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.650
And I thought it was some
sort of drill or something.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:08.090
And then everyone went outside
and flew open in the door

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.640
and there were about 150 people

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.760
waiting in the parking lot outside.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.760
Ton of my students from
mixed choir and orchestra,

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.800
school board members, the
Principal Fine Arts Director

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:18.890
and I pan across

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:21.870
and I see my parents had
flown in from Iowa, cousin,

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.095
my sister from New York, people
from DC, Nashville had come

00:02:25.095 --> 00:02:27.150
every which way and crossed paths.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:30.270
And right in that moment is
when they presented the award.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.930
- That is such a special way to do it.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:35.010
I love it so much.
(audience applauding)

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.588
And well deserved.

00:02:36.588 --> 00:02:39.990
Take it from a kid who
really like my junior-

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:43.090
literally my middle school
Choir Director changed my life.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.985
So she really is the one who pushed me,

00:02:44.985 --> 00:02:47.110
she took no crap from me being lazy.

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:48.530
She pushed me and it was awesome.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:49.870
It made me have the work ethic I have now

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:52.100
which is why we both have a billion jobs.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.080
But thank you, Katy.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.115
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:55.115 --> 00:02:56.160
(ding)

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.850
It's an amazing thing, y'all,
what teachers do for children.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:02:59.830
Thank you so much.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:00.663
And that's not all.

00:03:00.663 --> 00:03:03.370
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:04.890
the go-to pen of The Kelly Clarkson Show

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.950
want to honor ultimate
overachievers, just like you ma'am

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.780
so they're gonna write
you a cheque for $1,000

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:10.848
just cause you're cool.

00:03:10.848 --> 00:03:14.540
(audience cheering)
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.403
Thank you so much, Katy.

